/**
 * @file probeI.cnl
 *   Test case for linNet.\n
 * A current source and a current probe form a closed circuit.\n
 *   The current probe probeI creates a new calculated current. This current is not used
 * anywhere (e.g., to control a voltage or current source), but it becomes element of the
 * calculation result. (By default, only voltages are in an unspecified result.)\n
 *   This simple circuit may be useful to better understand the way how the orientation of
 * currents in sources and probes is defined.
 *
